### Forvo's brand

Forvo's visual identity is fragmented across its ecosystem — the app and website share an accent colour, but fonts, layout, and tone feel inconsistent throughout.

Branding wasn't the primary scope of this project, but it felt inseparable from the UX work. A platform asking users to trust its pronunciations and engage with its community needs to feel coherent and intentional.

The direction I explored: warm tones complementing Forvo's existing blue, playful communication alongside clear informative copy — friendly enough to feel welcoming, restrained enough to stay out of the way of learning.
